“IntelliJ IDEA is best for large, distributed codebases, even across enterprise architecture, as it understands links to other parts of the business.”
– CTO, E-commerce
Interviewees credited IntelliJ IDEA's understanding of dependencies across large, complex codebases for catching problems before they reach production. The Director of Software Engineering at a telecommunications company said their error rate "was also around 10% less when using IntelliJ IDEA, even before AI came."
Forrester also notes that code review becomes even more important as teams adopt AI-assisted development, since AI-generated code has to be validated against the same quality standards.
Productivity gains that continue to grow
Forrester found that IntelliJ IDEA improves developer productivity by up to 20%, defining productivity as faster pull request throughput and team-level efficiency gains, combined with less friction from consolidating tools and switching context. IntelliJ IDEA makes code creation 20% more efficient by years 2 and 3, saving the business $5.7 million. Interviewees also said the IDE's understanding of large codebases means developers avoid having to write additional code that other tools would require. One telecom engineering director said developers can now finish refactoring work in five hours instead of eight. Many of the features that make coding easier and more productive for developers writing code can also help developers using agents.
