An open approach to AI
Every interviewee highlighted IntelliJ IDEA's open approach to AI as a key benefit. Developers can use JetBrains AI tools and Junie alongside third-party models and agents directly inside the IDE, so teams can evaluate new tools as they appear or as models change and choose different ones for different tasks. In a market where models update constantly, this flexibility is critical to ensure developers can access the best tool for the job at any given moment. 
“IntelliJ IDEA serves as a stable platform so that we can adopt internal or third-party tools faster without disrupting current workflows.”
– Senior Software Engineer, Financial Services
Interviewees at organizations with high AI adoption reported large increases in output, with one CTO measuring a 10% to 40% boost in pull requests per developer per week. However, one head of engineering noted that while code creation with AI is much faster, review, debugging, and standardization are much slower, so the total time from presubmit to production is about the same. Forrester notes that because IntelliJ IDEA understands how code changes affect the rest of a project, it may help reduce the risks associated with AI-generated code, and embedded features could help alleviate those bottlenecks.
“IntelliJ IDEA can be fully deployed behind the firewall, including AI models, which enables work on sensitive telecom, billing, and network systems without having to expose data externally.”
