Where we're going next
The new bottlenecks around review and verification and threats to code quality are some of the key problems that JetBrains Air was built to address. Air is an open, coherent system of products for developers, teams, and organizations, inside and beyond JetBrains IDEs. Air in IntelliJ IDEA brings a complete agentic development experience into the IDE, where developers can direct agents and verify their output using the same code intelligence that Forrester's interviewees credited with higher code quality, context, and productivity. It supports the open, multi-vendor approach that Forrester highlights as a key advantage, and puts developers firmly in the driver’s seat.
If you’d like to learn more about the immediate business benefits of using IntelliJ IDEA, read the full Forrester TEI study.
This study was commissioned by JetBrains and delivered by Forrester Consulting. Results are based on a composite organization built from interviews with nine IntelliJ IDEA customers.
